{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>It shall not be poured.</b> With two yods — a hithpa'el form, like ״לְמַעַן יִיטַב לָךְ״ (Deuteronomy 5)." "<b>Upon the flesh of a man it shall not be poured.</b> From this very oil itself." "<b>And in its proportion you shall not make like it.</b> In the exact sum of its ingredients you shall not make another like it, in the weighting of these ingredients according to the measure of a hin of oil. But if he diminished or increased the ingredients in proportion to the measure of a hin of oil, it is permitted. And even one made in the exact proportion of this — the one who anoints from it is not liable, only the one who compounded it." "<b>And in its proportion.</b> A term of reckoning, like ״מַתְכֹּנֶת הַלְּבֵנִים״ (Exodus 5), and so too בְּמַתְכֻּנְתָּהּ of the incense."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:53.640700170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}